<xt>
  <!-- T-570 (improvement report F55): a `transform` timeline written rotate() before translate()
       goes through 05.5's compose/decompose path, whose identity rotateX/rotateY/translateZ tracks
       force is3D = 1 on #memo (19.3). Outside any 3D space root the node is flattened onto the 2D
       chain and drawn, so it must be hit tested through the same `world` too. #memo2 is the same
       intro written in the fixed order (never broken). -->
  <head>
    <style>
      @keyframes intro { from { transform: rotate(-4deg) translateY(-30px); } to { transform: rotate(-1deg) translateY(0px); } }
      @keyframes intro-fixed { from { transform: translateY(-30px) rotate(-4deg); } to { transform: translateY(0px) rotate(-1deg); } }
      #memo { position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 40px; width: 200px; height: 120px; background-color: #333333; animation: intro 0.5s forwards; }
      #memo2 { position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 180px; width: 200px; height: 120px; background-color: #333333; animation: intro-fixed 0.5s forwards; }
      #btn-restart, #btn-restart2 { position: absolute; left: 20px; top: 20px; width: 80px; height: 30px; background-color: #888888; }
      #btn-restart:hover, #btn-restart2:hover { background-color: #ff0000; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body id="root">
    <div id="memo"><div id="btn-restart" on:click="state(Clicked)"></div></div>
    <div id="memo2"><div id="btn-restart2" on:click="state(Clicked)"></div></div>
  </body>
</xt>
